      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(macos): local gateway auth fails when token is only in LaunchAgent env file",
        "body": "Related: #89967\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where macOS users running a shell-first gateway LaunchAgent could fail local attach or auth when the gateway token exists only in the generated service-env file, not in inline plist env or openclaw.json.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTeach `LaunchAgentPlist.snapshot` to read merged inline and generated env-file values and unwrap shell-first program arguments, matching daemon install/read behavior on the TypeScript side.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe mac app can recover `OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN` from the installed LaunchAgent again, so local connect and attach work without duplicating the token into config.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests`: shell-first plist plus env file resolves token/password and unwraps gateway args.\n- macOS IPC test target: `GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests`.\n",
